{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>יאחז</b> — The snare by his heel: the thirsty ones [plant-thirsty shoots?] gain strength upon him. And the priest [an epithet], may his memory be for a blessing, said: the maidens. And others say: in the language of Kedar, stones reversed, for 'the stones of the field are your covenant.'"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The identity of 'הכהן' is uncertain; left as 'the priest' per instructions to preserve standard epithets, though the referent is unclear. 'הצמאים' and 'הבתולות' appear to be variant readings of the verse text; both left untranslated in Hebrew as they are the subject of the dispute. The quotation at the end is from Job 5:23."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:57.849756908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}